A module on disk that the go.work deliberately omits. Discovery by filesystem walk
finds three modules; the module graph reports two. Which is right is policy, not
arithmetic: go.work says "these are the modules I am working on", so excluding it
may be intentional — or it may be the module someone forgot to add. The tool has to
pick a default and say which it picked.

modules_on_disk: 3
go_list_m: 2
go_list_dotdotdot: 1
discovered_modules: 3
discovered_packages: 3
packages_with_tests: 0
-- go.work --
go 1.27

use (
	.
	./included
)
-- go.mod --
module fixture.test/root

go 1.27
-- root.go --
package root

func R() int { return 1 }
-- included/go.mod --
module fixture.test/included

go 1.27
-- included/inc.go --
package included

func I() int { return 2 }
-- omitted/go.mod --
module fixture.test/omitted

go 1.27
-- omitted/omit.go --
package omitted

func O() int { return 3 }
